/-!
# Twenty-five vectors for the exact support {0,1}

The vectors are translates indexed by twenty coordinate line–plane flags
and five further flags. For each vector, a product of at most three upper-root
differences kills its predecessors and takes it to a nonzero translate.
The action entries are concrete binary matrix identities. The evaluations
are sums of the two active rank-one relations, transported by the stabilizer
identities in `FlagRelations`. Thus the triangular extraction criterion
proves independence for any module carrying the specified nonzero vector.

The generator and finite certificates are retained in `source/`.
Every matrix identity is checked by the Lean kernel; the generator is not
part of the trust boundary.

Source application: Guralnick–Malle, Classification of 2F-modules II,
Lemma 4.2/Table 6, pp.22–23, and Proposition 4.8(3B), pp.27–28;
Aschbacher–Smith K.3.2, printed pp.454–455.
-/

-- Generated uniform tactics serve expressions of different sizes.
